{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the waters covered the chariots and the horsemen, to all the army of Pharaoh</b> — Thus is the way of Scripture to speak with an extra ל (lamed), as in \"to all the utensils of the tabernacle\" (Exodus 27:19), \"for all its utensils you shall make bronze\" (Exodus 27:3), and it is nothing but an expression of specification. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 14:28). But this is not so in this place; rather, its meaning is: and they covered the chariots and the horsemen and all the army of Pharaoh who came after them into the sea. And the army is not the chariots and the horsemen, but rather they are his people whom he took with him, as it says above (Exodus 14:9), \"all the horse, the chariots of Pharaoh and his horsemen and his army.\" And like it is a covering with a ל (lamed): \"like the waters covering the sea\" (Isaiah 11:9), \"and you shall make a covering for the tent\" (Exodus 26:14), and with עַל it occurs: \"the covering upon the innards\" (Leviticus 4:8), and likewise many others."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:13.827640774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}